      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: By using `scope-\u003eGetValue(name.value())` (with only one argument), this resolves to the `const` version of `GetValue`, which **does not** mark the variable as used. \n\nAs a result, if a user imports a macro via `load()` and invokes it, GN\u0027s unused variable checker will still complain that the macro variable was never used and fail the build. \n\nYou should explicitly pass `true` to `counts_as_used` to use the non-const overload:\n```cpp\nconst Value* val \u003d scope-\u003eGetValue(name.value(), true);\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1662,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1662,
        "endChar": 0
