      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: Similar to template invocations, we should prevent target declarations and other nestable blocks inside the macro\u0027s argument block. Without this, users could accidentally (or intentionally) declare targets inside the `kwargs` block of a Starlark macro.\n\nConsider adding a `NonNestableBlock` here:\n```cpp\n        NonNestableBlock non_nestable(scope, function, \"macro invocation\");\n        if (!non_nestable.Enter(err))\n          return Value();\n```",
